The correct way to do this in Sails.js is to use the `actionGroups` option in the route configuration. Here's how you can do it:

```javascript
"post /rest/users": {
    controller: "FirstController",
    actionGroups: [{
        name: "userActions",
        actions: ["someAction", "otherAction"]
    }]
}
```

This way, both `someAction` and `otherAction` from `FirstController` will be executed for the `/rest/users` route. This is the recommended approach in Sails.js for handling multiple actions for the same route.

