Unfortunately, Room does not provide a built-in mechanism to throttle the rate at which observers are notified. However, you can implement a custom solution to achieve this. One approach is to use a `CountDownLatch` or a `Semaphore` to control the rate at which notifications are delivered to the observers.

Here's an example using a `CountDownLatch`:

```java
import java.util.concurrent.CountDownLatch;
import java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;

public class ThrottledObserver {
    private final CountDownLatch latch;
    private final Subscriber<? super T> subscriber;

    public ThrottledObserver(Subscriber<? super T> subscriber) {
        this.subscriber = subscriber;
        this.latch = new CountDownLatch(1);
    }

    public void observe(T t) {
        subscriber.onNext(t);
        latch.countDown();
    }

    public void unsubscribe() {
        subscriber.unsubscribe();
        latch.countDown(); // Make sure all notifications are delivered
    }
}

